    "finding": "The outer ring is EXACTLY 0.0 in every slice on all four sides, while column 1 — one cell in from the western edge — reaches p = 1.0. A probability field does not fall from 1.0 to exactly 0.0 across one cell, so the western edge is TRUNCATED, not resolved. But the core occupies columns 1-87 of 147 and rows 72-116 of 181, so it has room to grow east, north and south and does not. Truncation therefore explains the western boundary; it does NOT explain why the core is near-static.",
